WEBVTT

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.510
Poppy, shh.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.020
<i>Daily life in Japan.</i>

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:31.650
<i>Every morning, I check the mailbox to pick up</i>

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:34.400
<i>newspapers after I try to wake up Shino.</i>

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:37.790
<i>I wear a padded short coat when it's cold.</i>

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:41.070
<i>I also throw water in front
of the door in summer.</i>

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:44.790
<i>I greet Shino's mum and
Isami, and then I go to</i>

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:48.660
<i>Shino's room again to wake her
up if she's still asleep.</i>

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.380
<i>She has trouble getting up.</i>

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.550
Poppy, do you remember Shino?

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:58.630
Shi-no-bu, a Japanese middle school

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:01.340
student who did a homestay at our house.

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:03.680
She looked like a kokeshi doll.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:06.640
We call her Shino.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:07.680
Alice.

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:09.660
Shino!

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:12.190
I came to see you, Alice.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:14.680
Shino, I'm so happy!

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.240
Sigh

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:22.750
Alice, I'm tired of playing Shino.

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:25.330
Please, Karen! Just do it one more time!

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:58.770
You haven't stopped talking about

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:00.810
Shino since we arrived in England.

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:01.850
Well, I...

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:06.100
Karen, you've been filming lots of
videos since we arrived in England.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:07.930
Because I Love You
More Than Anything

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.760
Yes. I'm going to show everyone

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:10.630
the sights they're missing in Japan.

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:12.520
That's a great idea.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.290
You should shoot more buildings and...

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:15.190
No, no...

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:19.960
This is the "Depressed Alice
Misses Shino" video collection!

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:21.530
What even <i>is</i> that?

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:22.690
Okay, then...

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:25.510
Let's go buy gifts again today!

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:26.690
Let's go shopping!

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:29.450
We bought tons of gifts yesterday.
We have enough.

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:30.690
Aww!

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:34.500
Don't you think the greatest gift we
can give them is our safe return?

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:36.230
I see.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:38.800
But do you think Shino

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:40.750
will remember us?

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:43.130
Maybe she's already...

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:45.340
Sheesh

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:45.390
She'll remember!

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:48.730
She didn't forget when we were separated
for three years after her homestay!

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:51.490
This time, we're only apart for a week!

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:53.060
But the other day, Shino...

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:58.230
Copenhagen is the capital of which country?

00:03:58.540 --> 00:03:59.160
...said that.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.160
That's a normal memory lapse!

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:03.370
So you think Shino will remember us?

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:06.820
Yeah. And I'm sure she misses us, too.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.690
<i>Right, Shino?</i>

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:09.890
Alice!

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.110
<i>Shino!</i>

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:12.340
Alice!

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:14.030
How very interesting.

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:14.700
Very
interesting

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:14.700
Shino!

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:17.840
Shino, the model Japanese woman...

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:21.210
Alice, are you sure you
really remember Shino?

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.890
What do you want to do today?

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:25.970
We can do whatever you want.

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:27.050
Really?

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:28.800
Boar, deer, butterfly!

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.880
Man, you're too good at this.

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:34.430
I haven't played hanafuda in ages.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:38.670
I played hanafuda with
Shino in this room, too.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:43.520
Alice, do you want to call Shino?

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:44.100
Huh?

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:48.540
No. It's nighttime in Japan.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:50.570
Oh, right.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:54.940
I figured it must be inconvenient
for you and Shino,

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.310
not having cell phones.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:59.960
But even with one, it's still inconvenient.

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:04.310
If there's something you want to say,
you can write a letter.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:06.590
That's what Shino and I do.

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:10.940
But that takes a long time.

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:11.930
Oh, right.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:16.850
Alice, Karen. I'm making scones.

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:24.870
Karen is here!

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:27.610
I'm finished!

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:31.650
Let's make lots of hearts.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:35.700
Miss! Is this okay?

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:38.550
Yes. You're quite good at this, Karen.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.020
We made some at Shino's house, too.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:42.110
Really?

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:44.410
We all had a tea party.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:47.950
Shino was really excited, but we
took so long making everything,

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.720
we ended up eating them
at school the next day.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:54.850
We laid out a sheet in the courtyard.
It was like a picnic.

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:57.870
Your sesame cookies were good, Karen.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:00.690
Honoka and the other teachers
liked the cookies, too.

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:03.600
I borrowed Ayaya's cookie cutters
and made heart-shaped cookies.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:07.890
It was awful when Youko
spilled the flour everywhere.

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:09.820
Clumsy Youko!

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:13.250
And Shino spilled orange
juice before you got there.

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:14.630
Clumsy Shino!

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:20.270
Tell me more about Japan.

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:21.120
Okay!

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:42.790
They look delicious!

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:44.390
Yeah! Let's eat!

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:48.050
Let's eat.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:49.270
Let's dig in!

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:53.240
They're piping hot.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:57.950
There's ice cream, too.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:00.360
I want some!

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:05.420
Time flies. One week already passed.

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:09.000
Alice, your dad will give you a
ride to the airport tomorrow.

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:11.050
That's nice of him!

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:12.860
What about your parents, Karen?

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:14.680
I'm meeting them at the airport.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:18.300
This was your family vacation,
but you spent most of your time here.

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:20.810
I'll come back again with my parents.

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:24.560
Both of you seem to be getting
used to life in Japan.

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:28.110
You guys talk to each other in Japanese.

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:32.440
Besides, I can't believe you
eat "natto" every meal...

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:32.440
Kokeshi Natto

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:37.450
But I brought this all the way from Japan!

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:41.340
I hope we can all come
here together next time.

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:44.580
Yeah. I bet Aya doesn't like flying, though.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:47.890
If Youko comes, Ayaya's sure to follow.

00:07:47.890 --> 00:07:50.590
To the other side of the world,
or even into space.

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.520
Yeah!

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:54.030
I guess I have no choice.

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:55.090
Wow!

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:01.030
When we get back to Japan,
summer vacation will be over.

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:04.120
I'm excited for the second semester.
There are the sports and school festivals.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:06.020
And there's Shino Day, too.

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:08.090
We'll have to throw a party.

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:11.040
Yeah. I can't wait.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:12.510
Same here.

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:16.720
Made you yawn.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:19.690
Let's go to bed.

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:20.570
Okay.

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:27.120
Karen.

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:32.380
Thanks for inviting me to
come to England with you.

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:39.320
If we don't go to sleep now,
we won't be able to wake up.

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:41.000
I'm going to sleep.

00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:42.610
Goodnight.

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:44.600
Yeah. Goodnight.

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:52.650
I'm calling Japan.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:56.770
I didn't get to talk to Shino
the day I got here, but today...

00:08:56.770 --> 00:08:58.530
Your first conversation in a week.

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:00.200
You must be nervous.

00:09:00.530 --> 00:09:01.910
Your heart's pounding!

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:03.490
D-Don't do that, Karen.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.960
What should I do? My hands are shaking.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:11.810
Deep breaths, Alice!

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:14.830
<i>All this over a phone call?</i>

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:17.010
Yes, hello? Hello?

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:19.140
Oh, I see.

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:20.840
Then I'll take this one.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:24.410
Shino's at her limit.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:26.300
Should we go to bed?

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:27.020
Yeah.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.440
Alice-chan is on the phone.

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:31.770
Alice!

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:34.350
She woke up fast...

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:38.320
Alice, it's been so long!

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:40.010
How have you been?

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:41.900
I'm glad she finally got to talk to Alice.

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:43.830
Yeah. She seems happy—

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:45.600
Wait, she's frozen!

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:46.120
Could it be?

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.300
Did something happen to Alice?!

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.500
How are you, Shino? I'm fine.

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:50.580
Karen, Mum, Dad, and Poppy are also well.

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:52.370
Alice is talking really rapidly in English...

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:53.380
I'm leaving to catch the flight soon.
I'll be in Japan around...

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:53.380
Hiding your embarrassment?

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:54.960
...nine in the morning your time.

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:58.010
Karen and I've got tons of gifts
for you, so look forward to it.

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:01.070
I hope you'll like them.
I enjoyed being in the UK.

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:02.590
It brought me good memories.

00:10:02.590 --> 00:10:05.970
My mum and family were happy, too.
I'll tell you more when I get home.

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:11.520
I... I don't know what to say.

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:14.190
It's been such a long time.

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:15.190
Hello.

00:10:16.990 --> 00:10:18.530
H-Hello.

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:19.760
Hello.

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.100
It sounds like a conversation...

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.900
Hello, hello.

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:23.360
No way.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:27.330
Shino, s-sorry about that just now.

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:29.640
Alice, give me the phone.

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:30.410
Okay.

00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:32.810
Shino, how are you?

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:35.580
We bought tons of gifts,
so prepare yourself!

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:38.310
Yeah, Alice is doing well, too.

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:41.220
She said that being in England
brought back memories.

00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:44.260
Okay, bye.

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:47.610
What?! Why did you hang up?!

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:48.480
Sorry, I just—

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:50.430
"Just" nothing!

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:54.640
I hardly spoke to her at all...

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:56.930
But you were talking a ton, Alice.

00:10:56.930 --> 00:10:59.490
It's okay. I'm sure Shino understood.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:01.470
Y-Yeah...

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:06.980
It's too bad you couldn't talk to Alice again.

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:09.130
No, we talked this time.

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:11.610
Lots and lots, in English. We said "hello."

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:12.660
I see.

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:16.950
Did you forget anything?

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:18.770
Nope, that's everything.

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:28.320
Girls, it's time.

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:31.660
Coming.

00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:35.060
Thanks for everything.

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:39.060
Take good care of your health.
And take care of Alice.

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:41.140
Okay! Leave it to me!

00:11:41.140 --> 00:11:43.690
Sheesh, I'm not a child!

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:49.000
Come back home anytime.

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:49.590
Okay!

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:50.680
Bye!

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:07.860
I'll be waiting for your letters.

00:12:09.590 --> 00:12:10.500
Okay.

00:12:13.470 --> 00:12:14.720
See you soon.

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:31.700
Alice and Karen should be coming home soon.

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:35.950
But why is she in the bath?

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:44.650
Does anything look weird?

00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:47.150
Dressed Her Very Best

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:47.150
Only as weird as you always look.

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:48.960
It's nearly time!

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:50.470
You're waiting outside?

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:55.890
Alice!

00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:57.230
Shino!

00:12:57.230 --> 00:12:59.490
Alice! Karen!

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:01.760
I'm home, Shino!

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:03.340
I'm home!

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:08.340
Welcome home. I'm glad you returned safely.

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:10.490
Squeeze

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:10.490
It was such a long week.

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:12.170
Welcome back.

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:13.130
Welcome back.

00:13:13.130 --> 00:13:14.450
We're back!

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:15.620
You came, too?

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:18.070
Yes. We didn't get to see you off, so...

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:20.330
By the way, what's with the ribbons?

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:21.960
They're gifts.

00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:25.090
Why are you acting like <i>you're</i> the gifts?

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:28.460
We bought lots for all of you, too.

00:13:28.460 --> 00:13:30.360
Take whatever you want.

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:32.310
Oh, wow!

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:34.710
Is this tea? It's so cute.

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:35.890
It's Earl Grey.

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:39.260
Welcome back.

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:40.420
Isami!

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:41.900
Isami, choose a gift.

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:44.400
I'll choose last.

00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:53.720
I'm Oomiya Shinobu.

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:57.910
This is the "Depressed Alice
Misses Shino" video collection.

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:03.780
Alice is super depressed right now.

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:06.830
I'll cheer her up by pretending to be Shino.

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:09.070
Not that!

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:12.710
Do you have jet lag?

00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:14.640
No. I slept on the plane.

00:14:21.860 --> 00:14:24.190
While you were gone,

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:26.400
I was so lonely, I cried a little.

00:14:26.790 --> 00:14:28.290
Shino...

00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:31.610
Tell me about your time in England.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:32.810
Okay.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:38.770
<i>Huh? Shino's summer
homework is all blank.</i>

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:41.800
<i>She said she'd finish it while I was gone.</i>

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:42.120
White

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:46.870
Shino, you might end up crying
for a different reason soon.

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:47.580
Huh?

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:51.840
Hello!!
Kin-iro Mosaic

00:14:52.550 --> 00:14:55.340
Hello!!
Kin-iro Mosaic

00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:58.150
What?

00:14:58.650 --> 00:15:01.140
She finished her summer
homework this morning?

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:01.770
Yeah.

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:04.110
The deadline is today.

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:06.700
I thought she'd be okay with you around.

00:15:06.950 --> 00:15:08.820
I couldn't be of help.

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:12.450
Shino never changes.

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:13.950
Blonde Girl Club

00:15:16.320 --> 00:15:18.210
Shinobu-chan, you dropped—

00:15:19.510 --> 00:15:20.810
I-I'm sorry!

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:22.090
I didn't see anything!

00:15:22.090 --> 00:15:25.060
It was hidden under a mosaic!

00:15:25.060 --> 00:15:26.220
What happened?

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:30.220
Shino, what is this?

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:32.410
My English test.

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:33.720
I can see that!

00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:35.900
You need to buckle down and study!

00:15:35.900 --> 00:15:38.420
We start studying for entrance
exams in six months!

00:15:38.420 --> 00:15:41.470
Ayaya, don't be so hard on Shino.

00:15:41.470 --> 00:15:42.230
Karen?

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:45.050
She may not be good at studying,

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:47.690
but Shino has many talents.

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:50.690
Even if she only scored five points on her test!

00:15:50.690 --> 00:15:52.580
Karen, not so loud.

00:15:54.190 --> 00:15:56.120
What kinds of talents?

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:58.280
Well, she can spin plates.

00:15:58.280 --> 00:15:59.640
Twirl, twirl, twirl.

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:01.720
I've never spun plates.

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:04.140
That's okay. It's pretty easy.

00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:05.810
Then maybe I can...

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:10.460
It broke before you even started.

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:11.590
The plate...

00:16:11.590 --> 00:16:12.740
No worries!

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:14.430
Next up is ventriloquism.

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:17.230
Why are they all party tricks?

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:19.850
Alice, you have such
beautiful blonde hair.

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:21.230
Thank you, Aya.

00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:23.110
I'll be taking that.

00:16:23.110 --> 00:16:25.450
Your hair tastes like honey.

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:28.030
Don't make me weird!

00:16:28.030 --> 00:16:29.610
And your mouth is totally moving!

00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:33.200
Gloom

00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:33.610
So I don't have any talents.

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:36.620
No one succeeds on their first try.

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:38.810
Let's try spinning plates again.

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:40.250
No, that's enough of that!

00:16:40.820 --> 00:16:42.380
Hello.

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:44.880
Oh! Even Youko's depressed.

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:46.630
What's wrong, Youko?

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:49.630
I prefer you full of energy.

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:51.830
Aya-chan's doing ventriloquism.

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:52.890
She's great at it.

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:56.640
Well, I broke Mitsuki's Kumao yesterday.

00:16:57.210 --> 00:16:58.390
Oh, no!

00:16:59.760 --> 00:17:01.870
Sorry. It wasn't on purpose.

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:03.540
That's a sloppy repair job!

00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:07.300
Onee-chan... Onee-chan broke...

00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:08.480
There, there.

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:11.030
Mitsuki, I'm sorry! I shouldn't
have used duct tape.

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:13.010
I should at least have
used cellophane tape.

00:17:14.440 --> 00:17:17.820
Why am I so boorish?

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:20.990
It's okay. Kumao-san's all better.

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:21.410
What?

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:24.420
Here. Now you can make up with them.

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:26.790
You did that in a second?

00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:29.210
Thank you! You're the best, Shino!

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:31.700
Of course she is. She's Shino.

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:32.830
Shino's the greatest!

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:34.320
Shino's the greatest!

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:36.120
You're exaggerating.

00:17:36.470 --> 00:17:38.600
You do have a talent.

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:42.560
You could grow up to be a
professional clothing designer.

00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:45.570
Oh, yeah! Shino, you're going to be a designer!

00:17:45.570 --> 00:17:47.450
A designer? That's cool!

00:17:47.450 --> 00:17:49.900
Wow! You'll be internationally famous!

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:54.160
But I want to be an interpreter...

00:17:55.230 --> 00:17:56.160
Shino.

00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:58.530
Everyone has their strengths and weaknesses.

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:01.040
A single blow from Alice...

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:03.490
But if you work hard,

00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:05.540
I'll support you with all I've got.

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:08.290
Alice...

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:11.790
If it still doesn't work out,
I'll become an interpreter.

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:13.880
What would be the point in that?

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:17.280
All right. I'll work hard.

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:19.520
You can do it, Shino!

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:22.140
I'll support you with everything I've got!

00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:24.140
It's time to study.

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:28.240
Define and write 50 English
vocabulary terms 50 times each!

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:30.210
Alice, you're too strict.

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:31.520
Can't we just do ten?

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:33.190
We're going hard today!

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:35.060
Hard! Hard! Hard!

00:18:36.150 --> 00:18:40.240
Nothing sticks unless you're
actually motivated to study.

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:43.920
Dangling carrots in front
of horses motivates them.

00:18:43.920 --> 00:18:45.610
So Shino needs blonde hair.

00:18:46.240 --> 00:18:48.420
How are we going to dangle blonde hair?

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:49.290
Here we go.

00:18:51.050 --> 00:18:52.270
What's going on?

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:53.630
It's motivating her, though.

00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:56.260
They say you excel at
things that interest you.

00:18:56.510 --> 00:18:59.650
You're not good at English,
but you like foreign nations.

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:01.260
So you'll be fine.

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:02.940
Youko-chan...

00:19:03.310 --> 00:19:07.020
Yes. I love Alice and Karen.

00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:10.630
And you're a glutton because you love food.

00:19:10.630 --> 00:19:11.280
I see.

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:13.030
That's just my appetite!

00:19:33.830 --> 00:19:38.950
I finished all the review sheets by myself!

00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:40.220
That's actually normal.

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:43.190
I feel so much smarter now.

00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:45.030
Thank you, everyone.

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:46.480
You worked really hard.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:48.850
Basic High School
English Problems

00:19:46.900 --> 00:19:49.370
Now, on to the next set of problems!

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:50.600
Let's give it one more push!

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:52.480
Please spare me!

00:19:58.100 --> 00:20:00.650
My brain feels foggy from too much use.

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:02.990
Your brain's always foggy.

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:05.640
Want to stop by someplace?

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:07.780
Yes! I want crêpes!

00:20:07.780 --> 00:20:08.850
Crêpes!

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:11.050
Good idea. That's what young people do.

00:20:11.050 --> 00:20:12.580
I want chocolate custard.

00:20:12.580 --> 00:20:13.850
Chocolate marron!

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:16.260
I want something with strawberries.

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:17.710
It's so hard to choose.

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:19.020
What about you, Aya-chan?

00:20:19.020 --> 00:20:22.010
Well, maybe I'll get the apple cinnamon.

00:20:22.010 --> 00:20:24.010
That sounds good. Let me have a bite.

00:20:24.010 --> 00:20:24.890
Huh?

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:26.860
You can have some of mine, too.

00:20:27.310 --> 00:20:28.140
It's a promise.

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:31.520
You always just do as you please...

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:38.120
The evening sun's so bright.

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:40.590
All right! We didn't have PE today,

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:42.370
so let's race there!

00:20:42.370 --> 00:20:42.930
What?

00:20:42.930 --> 00:20:43.930
Okay.

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:45.540
Run!

00:20:45.540 --> 00:20:46.330
Okay!

00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:47.920
Wait, Shino!

00:20:47.920 --> 00:20:49.540
Go, go!

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:52.290
W-Wait!

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:54.850
Youth...

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:55.550
Huh?

00:20:56.030 --> 00:20:58.260
Being young is great, isn't it?

00:20:58.260 --> 00:21:01.920
When I was a student, all I did was study.

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:04.430
I didn't really get to enjoy my youth.

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:08.810
Kuzehashi-sensei, you're always
young if you're having fun.

00:21:09.320 --> 00:21:10.880
Karasuma-sensei...

00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:13.040
Let's try a high five for old times' sake.

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:13.560
Huh?

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:16.500
High five!

00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:15.940
H-High...

00:21:16.070 --> 00:21:16.820
Fwish

00:21:17.140 --> 00:21:19.240
That didn't go very well.

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:22.320
Karasuma-sensei...

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:25.950
Shall we try it again?

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:28.590
Here we go.

00:21:28.590 --> 00:21:29.640
Totem...

00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:30.460
...pole!

00:21:32.920 --> 00:21:33.750
Golden!

00:21:34.110 --> 00:21:34.710
Hair!

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:36.460
Meow, meow.

00:21:36.780 --> 00:21:38.710
I'm sending this to Honoka.

00:21:38.710 --> 00:21:41.590
Mitsuki! Shino fixed him.

00:21:41.930 --> 00:21:45.470
Thanks. The stitching is beautiful.

00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:46.810
Isn't it?

00:21:46.810 --> 00:21:48.980
Why are you so happy?

00:21:48.980 --> 00:21:50.100
Oh...

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:52.700
I was just really happy.

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:54.850
I'm sure Shino can become an interpreter.

00:21:55.130 --> 00:21:58.830
I've known her since we were
kids, so I must be right.

00:21:58.830 --> 00:22:00.680
I don't get what you're saying...

00:22:00.680 --> 00:22:02.280
But you sound like her mother.

00:22:02.280 --> 00:22:05.740
Really? Well, Shino's like a younger sister to me.

00:22:06.180 --> 00:22:07.440
A younger sister?

00:22:08.180 --> 00:22:11.250
Shouldn't you be worrying
about yourself first?

00:22:11.450 --> 00:22:12.620
Can't criticize the grades of others

00:22:12.860 --> 00:22:15.630
Mitsuki, you're still mad? Come on!

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:17.750
<i>She's jealous.</i>

00:22:17.750 --> 00:22:19.500
Inokuma Youko

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:23.510
I wonder if Youko made up with Mitsuki-chan.

00:22:27.100 --> 00:22:29.140
I can't do it!

00:22:29.470 --> 00:22:32.490
Isami, the girls are coming home soon.

00:22:32.490 --> 00:22:34.300
Help me make dinner.

00:22:34.300 --> 00:22:35.650
Sure...

00:22:36.950 --> 00:22:38.430
It's airmail.

00:22:38.860 --> 00:22:40.960
It's from your mother.

00:22:40.960 --> 00:22:42.970
I wonder if it's pictures of England.

00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:45.030
I can't wait to see them.

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:50.030
Alice, when you write a response,
can I write something, too?

00:22:50.290 --> 00:22:50.940
Huh?

00:22:51.360 --> 00:22:54.040
I'd like to try writing a letter in English.

00:22:54.300 --> 00:22:58.050
I'll be using a dictionary,
so it'll take some time.

00:22:58.050 --> 00:23:00.550
But it's my first step toward
becoming an interpreter.

00:23:00.550 --> 00:23:02.920
Okay. I'll help you.

00:23:03.160 --> 00:23:06.040
Okay. I'll start with a rough draft in romaji.

00:23:06.040 --> 00:23:09.250
You should write it in Japanese
and translate it into English.

00:23:09.250 --> 00:23:10.200
Really?

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:12.740
I thought my first airmail should be in romaji...
